# references.bib provenance log — Paper 2

Every entry in `references.bib` was verified on **2026-05-26** against an
authoritative metadata source (PubMed via NCBI E-utilities, JSTOR for the
pre-1990 statistics paper, NEJM AI for the BiomedCLIP peer-reviewed upgrade,
JOSS for the Pingouin software paper, Wiley for the Hosmer book, and arXiv
for the unpublished preprint). This file exists so that any reviewer, editor,
or subsequent author can spot-check the citation list field-by-field against
the same authoritative URLs the verification used.

Verification protocol (binding for any future bib edits):
1. Every BibTeX field (year, volume, issue, pages, first-author surname,
   journal name, DOI) is sourced from one of the URLs below; no field is
   taken from memory or any unverified source.
2. New entries added in any future revision must be appended to this log
   with the same provenance line format and date-stamped.
3. If an entry cannot be verified against an authoritative endpoint, it is
   marked UNVERIFIED and held out of the bibliography pending user action,
   not appended speculatively.

The verification pass that produced this log is documented in
`../decisions.log` entry #024 (2026-05-26).

